+---
+id: task-002-created-and-updated-timestamps-on-tasks
+type: task
+title: "Created and updated timestamps on tasks"
+status: approved
+format: 1
+---
+
+# Created and updated timestamps on tasks
+
+The app shows how old a task is, and what changed recently, so each task records when it was created
+and when it was last changed.
+
+## What to build
+
+- Every task has `createdAt` and `updatedAt`, ISO-8601 date-time strings.
+- When a task is added, `createdAt` and `updatedAt` are the same.
+- Every change to a task sets its `updatedAt` to the time of the change: completing, reopening,
+  renaming, tagging and untagging it.
+- The domain does not read the clock: the time comes from the list's caller. The app's
+  `createTodoList` uses the system clock; it accepts another clock, so tests can fix the time.
+
+## Acceptance
+
+- `add` returns a task whose `createdAt` equals its `updatedAt`, both ISO-8601 date-time strings.
+- Each change (complete, reopen, rename, tag, untag) sets `updatedAt` to the time of that change and
+  leaves `createdAt` as it was.
+- A change that does not alter the task (renaming to the same title, tagging with a tag it already
+  has, untagging a tag it lacks) leaves `updatedAt` unchanged.
